      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T03:55:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`sizeof(*resp) + kMaxChunkPayloadSize` \u003d 12 + 240 \u003d 252 bytes, but HECI only gives the handler 248 bytes on ToT (`HECI_CROS_EC_RESPONSE_MAX` 256 - 8 bytes of `ec_host_response`). When `max_size` is 0 or \u003e\u003d 237, the `memcpy` writes 4 bytes past `response_buffer`, and then `host_packet_respond()` fails with `EC_RES_RESPONSE_TOO_BIG`.\n\nMy CL:8612752 grows the HECI buffers to 280 (268 bytes for the handler), so it fits after that lands.\n\nEither way, 240 is a magic number that happens to fit. The legacy shim doesn\u0027t check the min request/response sizes, so check `args-\u003einput_buf_size \u003c sizeof(*params)` and `args-\u003eoutput_buf_max \u003c sizeof(*resp)`, and clamp `max_payload` to `args-\u003eoutput_buf_max - sizeof(*resp)`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 442,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 442,
        "endChar": 43
      },
